        "answer": {
          "short": "i. $y$: $4,1,0,1,4$.\n\nii. Upward-opening parabola with vertex $(-1,0)$; see sketch.\n\niii. Domain: $(-\\infty,\\infty)$. Range: $[0,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "Substitution gives\n$$\\begin{align*}y(-3)&=(-3)^2+2(-3)+1=4\\\\y(-2)&=(-2)^2+2(-2)+1=1\\\\y(-1)&=(-1)^2+2(-1)+1=0\\\\y(0)&=0^2+2(0)+1=1\\\\y(1)&=1^2+2(1)+1=4\\end{align*}$$\nPlot $(-3,4),(-2,1),(-1,0),(0,1),(1,4)$ and join them with a smooth upward-opening parabola, continuing both ends. The graph extends through every real $x$ and has minimum height $0$ at $x=-1$. Thus the domain is $(-\\infty,\\infty)$ and the range is $[0,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p12-q4-a-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"PDF page 12 Question 4a; teacher PDF page 8\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.65cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (-4,0)--(2.3,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-0.8)--(0,6) node[above] {$y$};\n\\foreach \\x in {-3,-2,-1,1}{\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (\\x,0.08)--(\\x,-0.08) node[below] {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\x$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\foreach \\y in {1,4}{\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0.08,\\y)--(-0.08,\\y) node[left] {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\y$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.8pt,domain=-3.35:1.35,samples=100] plot (\\x,{(\\x+1)^2});\n\\foreach \\x/\\y in {-3/4,-2/1,-1/0,0/1,1/4}{\\fill (\\x,\\y) circle (1.5pt);}\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
